---
source: crates/zeff-engine/tests/columns.rs
expression: all
---
## no_such_column (exit 1)
error[Z0101]: no variable `wge` in `w`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:3
  |
2 | w["wge"]
  |   ^^^^^ not a variable of w
  |
  = help: did you mean `wage`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"wage"`

## column_named_without_quotes (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: a frame's column is named in quotes: `["wage"]`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:3
  |
2 | w[wage]
  |   ^^^^ a bare name
  |
  = help: inside a frame method the bare name names the column; between brackets it is text

## column_named_by_a_number (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: a frame's column is named in quotes, but this is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:3
  |
2 | w[2]
  |   ^ an Int
  |
  = help: write `wages["lwage"]`; inside a frame method, the bare name `lwage` names the column

## different_lengths (exit 1)
error[Z0217]: columns of 3 and 2 rows cannot be combined
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:1
  |
3 | w["id"] + d["x"]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ two lengths
  |
  = help: combine columns of one frame, or of frames with the same rows; `merge` joins frames (release 0.6.0)

## int_overflow_in_a_row (exit 1)
error[Z0211]: Int overflow in row 2: 9223372036854775807 + 1 does not fit in 64 bits
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | d["x"] + 1
  | ^^^^^^^^^^ the operation
  |
  = help: Ints are 64-bit; a Float column (`1.0 * x`) holds larger magnitudes with 53 bits of precision

## text_column_in_arithmetic (exit 1)
error[Z0215]: `+` does not apply to text
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | w["name"] + 1
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the operation, row by row
  |
  = help: `join` puts texts together and `format` builds text from values (release 0.5.0); a number in text converts with `to(x, Float)`

## bool_column_in_arithmetic (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `*` needs numbers, but one side is a Bool
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | w["flag"] * 2
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the operation, row by row
  |
  = help: Bool is not a number; `to(x, Int)` turns true and false into 1 and 0

## comparing_column_types (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `==` compares values of one type, but these are text and a number
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | w["name"] == 1
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the operation, row by row
  |
  = help: Int and Float compare as numbers; text compares with text and Bool with Bool

## logic_on_a_number_column (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `&&` needs two Bools, but one side is a number
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | w["id"] && true
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the operation, row by row
  |
  = help: `&&` and `||` combine comparisons, as in `age > 18 && female`

## range_of_a_column (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `..` needs two Ints, not a column
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | 1..w["id"]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^ a column
  |
  = help: a range runs from one whole number to another: `2..5`

## date_column (exit 1)
error[Z0221]: `==` is not defined for this value
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | d["sold"] == d["sold"]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the operation, row by row
  |
  = help: comparison is for numbers, text, Bool and NA

